      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: rules of the road, part one",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: rules of the road, part one\nAudience: every first-time Tennessee Class D or learner permit applicant; this is the core of the rules of the road topic on the knowledge test.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: speed limits [A03], school bus and railroad stops [A07] and right-of-way at intersections [A10] are everyday legal duties and frequent test material.\nLevel: heavy rule recall with many exact distances, times, speeds and fines plus scenario judgment on who yields; the densest chapter so far.\nPrerequisites: the vehicle setup and signs and signals chapters, which introduce braking, stop lines and signal meanings used here.\n",
